}, "3": {"max_beta_per_topic": [0.9993, 0.9645, 0.3412], "mean_max_beta": 0.7683, "n_vertex_topics": 2}, "4": {"max_beta_per_topic": [0.9998, 0.9801, 0.8326, 0.4238], "mean_max_beta": 0.8091, "n_vertex_topics": 2}, "5": {"max_beta_per_topic": [0.9993, 0.9866, 0.9787, 0.8441, 0.735], "mean_max_beta": 0.9087, "n_vertex_topics": 3}, "8": {"max_beta_per_topic": [1.0, 0.9999, 0.9989, 0.9985, 0.9979, 0.951, 0.6314, 0.6262], "mean_max_beta": 0.9005, "n_vertex_topics": 6}}, "n_documents": 93804, "features": [{"key": "topic_1", "label": "LDA topic T1 weight", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.15183009881384213, "mean": 0.3603946994233702, "sd": 0.1435033438040387}, {"key": "topic_5", "label": "LDA topic T5 weight", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.16452078852156682, "mean": 0.20142135445159584, "sd": 0.17251611809600104}, {"key": "topic_4", "label": "LDA topic T4 weight", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.5131709497301182, "mean": 0.13801051975771395, "sd": 0.09890396604499943}, {"key": "tls_max", "label": "LDA topic T2 max over fields (TLS presence)", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.630295566173809, "mean": 0.7286491283501675, "sd": 0.23844423072862014}, {"key": "tls_mean", "label": "LDA topic T2 mean weight (mixed membership)", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.9379937966844054, "mean": 0.09891262474709395, "sd": 0.07398844646018185}, {"key": "topic_2", "label": "LDA topic T2 weight", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.9379937966844054, "mean": 0.09891262474709395, "sd": 0.07398844646018185}, {"key": "topic_3", "label": "LDA topic T3 weight", "kind": "soft", "p": 0.9475724418759759, "mean": 0.2012607734046749, "sd": 0.1012552659148691}, {"key": "niche_8", "label": "Hard k-means niche N8 fraction (B-cell aggregate)", "kind": "hard", "p": 0.9788695588781101, "mean": 0.07559076063301146, "sd": 0.08725806488548644}], "n_perm": 1000, "observed_min_p": 0.15183009881384213, "fwer_p": 0.585, "hard_vs_soft_corr": 0.9641, "hard_key": "niche_8", "soft_key": "tls_mean", "tls_topic": 2, "verdict": "Mixed membership does not rescue a TLS survival signal here. The soft topic weight (p = 0.938) and the hard niche fraction (p = 0.979) are both null, and they are close to the same variable anyway (r = 0.964). Across the whole family of 8 topic features the smallest p is 0.1518 with a family-wise permutation p of 0.58. But this is a weak test of TopSpace, because plain LDA at K = 5 on a six-type vocabulary degenerates to one topic per cell type (3 of 5 topics are >90% a single type), so its 'TLS topic' is really just a B-cell topic. What this shows is that the mixed-membership machinery alone does not produce a multicellular TLS structure; TopSpace's spatial prior is doing the work, and testing its claim properly needs its implementation, not this baseline.", "reference": "Choi J, Kang J, Baladandayuthapani V. arXiv:2504.18495. The abstract reports that TopSpace's TLS spatial probability correlates with survival on this cohort; the preprint's survival analysis details were not available to compare against directly."}, "patients": [{"patient": "#01 0-889-121", "tls_mean": 0.0444, "tls_max": 0.71381, "topic_1": 0.56679, "topic_2": 0.0444, "topic_3": 0.09014, "topic_4": 0.11253, "topic_5": 0.18614, "niche_8": 0.03048, "mhcII_status": "low", "survival_status": 0.0, "survival_days": 3488.0}, {"patient": "#02 1-037-393", "tls_mean": 0.13696, "tls_max": 0.92696, "topic_1": 0.14378, "topic_2": 0.13696, "topic_3": 0.33968, "topic_4": 0.05679, "topic_5": 0.32278, "niche_8": 0.11003, "mhcII_status": "low", "survival_status": 1.0, "survival_days": 1605.0}, {"patient": "#03 2-080-378", "tls_mean": 0.13337, "tls_max": 0.96364, "topic_1": 0.40769, "topic_2": 0.13337, "topic_3": 0.12333, "topic_4": 0.28729, "topic_5": 0.04831, "niche_8": 0.08787, "mhcII_status": "high", "survival_status": 1.0, "survival_days": 176.0}, {"patient": "#04 2-223-153", "tls_mean": 0.17846, "tls_max": 0.87273, "topic_1": 0.1898, "topic_2": 0.17846, "topic_3": 0.08688, "topic_4": 0.01965, "topic_5": 0.5252, "niche_8": 0.11683, "mhcII_status": "low", "surv